10152	{"artifactId":"LLD-a832f5b2560d917f-s1","entry":{"id":"review-1963aac4de210e99b9d32cdc9e8b04cd","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-30T04:21:40.638Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design's scope (remove signature/key verification, keep all other runtime/canonical checks, reject a new daemon-private attestation store) matches the user's explicit direction captured in citation c3.","evidence":"LLD body references '[[c3]] stakeholder user:2026-10-30 — \"point 1 I get, point 2 is overengineering\"'. Section 7 lists alternative a2 (new daemon-private attestation registry) as considered and rejected ('introduces an unnecessary new authority store and lifecycle'), consistent with the user calling that approach overengineering; the chosen a1 removes only the signature/key path, matching 'point 1'.","action":"none — matches recorded stakeholder direction","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Acceptance criteria ac1/ac2/ac3 are concretely defined and mapped to tests even though no upstream ISSUE/SPEC exists for this standalone feature.","evidence":"LLD-a832f5b2560d917f-s1.json meta.sizeClass='feature', standalone:true, triageRationale present; body.testStrategy.acceptanceMapping defines criterionId ac1/ac2/ac3 each with concrete provingTests naming exactly what must be proven (unsigned-probe acceptance, refusal of draft/stale/tampered evidence, and runbook update) — sufficient self-contained acceptance definition for a standalone feature-size story that has no separate ISSUE/SPEC artifact.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today, review-investigation-adoption.ts requires a cryptographic signature on the installed-probe report, verified against an external trust-anchor PEM file, and this is wired through a verifyProbe injection seam in InvestigationAdoptionDeps.","evidence":"src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts: probeSchema requires signature:z.string().min(1).max(4096) (line 33); verifyInstalledProbeSignature() reads keyPath=join(PATHS.insrc,'review-probe-trust.pem') and calls node:crypto verify() (lines 65-66); InvestigationAdoptionDeps.verifyProbe is an optional injection seam defaulted to verifyInstalledProbeSignature at call sites in evidence() (line 90) and assertQualified's verifyInstalled callback (line 109).","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"qualifyInvestigationAdapter's verifyInstalled callback is invoked on every qualification and every re-qualification (exactly the 'every use' claim), and separately validates identity, ACK/cancel ordering and expiry regardless of signature.","evidence":"src/agent/providers/investigation-session.ts: qualifyInvestigationAdapter() calls authority.verifyInstalled(reference,evidenceDigest) when authority.origin==='installed-probe' (line 112); the same check re-runs inside the later re-qualification path (line 139); inspectIsolationData() independently enforces ACK sequence/cancel/exit ordering (lines 96-98) and identity/catalog/launch digest checks (lines 88-89), none of which depend on the signature.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"readApprovedEvidence/approvedEvidenceReference, described as the 'existing canonical approval validation' the new unsigned path relies on, already exist with the stated approve/draft/stale/digest-match behaviour — nothing new is being introduced for canonical gating.","evidence":"src/daemon/review-investigation-approval.ts lines 10-13: approvedEvidenceReference() builds `approved:<id>@<revision>#<digest>`; readApprovedEvidence() refuses with 'Readiness evidence is missing, draft, stale or edited' when the head is absent, revision mismatches, approval state isn't 'approved', or the reference digest doesn't match — exactly the canonical-approval authority the design says it is reusing (no new store).","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The call sites listed for removing verifyInstalledProbeSignature/verifyProbe (review-investigation-adoption.ts and its test file, plus investigation-session.ts) are the complete set of references to these symbols in the codebase.","evidence":"Grep for verifyInstalledProbeSignature|probeSchema|verifyProbe across src/ returns exactly src/daemon/review-investigation-adoption.ts and src/daemon/__tests__/review-investigation-adoption.test.ts — matching the LLD's 3.1/3.2 call-site lists; no other production or script file (including scripts/review-investigation-probe.mjs) references these symbols.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The readiness/probe envelope shapes actually have the cardinality the design claims (one backendRef per source mode, one evidence snapshot per probe), so loosening `signature` to optional is a compatible superset that doesn't require a migration/rewrite.","evidence":"readinessSchema.backendRefs is z.object({'source-only':text,'indexed-impact':text}).strict() — exactly one ref per mode; probeSchema.evidence is a single z.unknown() parsed via snapshotValue into one NativeIsolationEvidence. Making `signature` optional (vs. the current required string) is a strict loosening that still accepts every existing stored record, so 'old signed records need no rewrite' holds structurally.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The code this design modifies (InvestigationAdoptionPolicy / verifyInstalledProbeSignature / probeSchema in review-investigation-adoption.ts) is not a shared contract formally owned by any Story of Epic c32aa60534232f36 (review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation), so a standalone LLD may redesign it without an HLD amendment.","evidence":"HLD-c32aa60534232f36.json storyBoundaries lists only sc1..sc7 as owned contracts (s1 owns sc1/sc6, s2 owns sc2, s3 owns sc3, s4 owns sc4, s5 owns sc5, s6 owns sc7/ReviewClientStatusV1 only); none of those interface sketches reference verifyInstalledProbeSignature, probeSchema, or InvestigationAdoptionPolicy. That mechanism was itself added later by a separate standalone story (ISSUE/LLD-7aaf7e1b4a54e86f-s1, standalone:true, not an amendment to c32aa60534232f36), establishing the repo's own precedent that this code is edited via standalone stories rather than epic-owned contracts.","action":"none — verified against HLD storyBoundaries and sharedContracts; not a declared cross-story contract","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The claimed detection path for a raw/unsigned/draft/stale/edited canonical probe (readApprovedEvidence rejecting missing current approval/revision/hash/history mismatch) matches the real refusal implementation.","evidence":"src/daemon/review-investigation-approval.ts line 13: readApprovedEvidence refuses with 'Readiness evidence is missing, draft, stale or edited' precisely on head-missing, revision mismatch, non-approved state, or reference-digest mismatch — matching the design's 'Raw unsigned export, draft, stale or edited canonical probe submitted' detection claim.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The edge case 'Approved report changes after qualification → verifyInstalled callback reloads canonical reference and refuses stale/different digest' matches the real re-qualification code path.","evidence":"review-investigation-adoption.ts line 109: assertQualified re-runs `const current=await this.evidence(mode)` (re-reading canonical evidence fresh) and its verifyInstalled callback refuses with 'Probe authority binding changed' if the reference or digestValue(current.evidence) differ from what was originally qualified — exactly the reload-and-refuse-on-change behaviour the design states.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac3's proving test ('Operator prerequisites and runbook omit signer/trust-key provisioning...') targets real, currently-existing operator documentation that does describe signer/trust-key provisioning today, so there is a real artifact to update and test against.","evidence":"docs/review-investigation.md lines 58 and 169-177 currently instruct provisioning 'the independently provisioned Ed25519 public trust anchor `~/.insrc/review-probe-trust.pem`' and describe the daemon never receiving the private key — exactly the content ac3's smoke test must verify has been removed/updated, and Migration step 1 explicitly includes 'update operator prerequisites/runbook'.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-30T04:21:40.638Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
